    <string name="manager_deploy_xposed_title">Xposed framework</string>
    <string name="manager_deploy_xposed_description">Enable NukeApp-OSS in a framework that supports XP82 or libxposed API 102, select the target apps in its scope, then fully restart them.</string>
    <string name="manager_deploy_root_title">Root manager (Zygisk)</string>
    <string name="manager_deploy_root_description">Export the module APK or copy the built one, change its extension from .apk to .zip, install it in Magisk or another root manager, enable Zygisk and reboot. Only arm64-v8a is supported.</string>
    <string name="manager_deploy_patch_title">APK patching</string>
    <string name="manager_deploy_patch_description">In the separate NukePatcher app, choose the exported module APK and the target APK, then install the patched output. The patcher does not need NukeApp-OSS installed.</string>

    <string name="manager_scope_fixture">Test host</string>
    <string name="manager_scope_tiktok">Douyin</string>
    <string name="manager_scope_settings">Douyin feature switches are under the NukeApp-OSS entry in Douyin\'s settings. Changes take effect after Douyin restarts.</string>
    <string name="manager_modes_explanation">The first entry to take effect in a process owns it; the others skip, so this module never hooks twice. After a failed start the host must be restarted; the entry never switches on its own.</string>

    <string name="manager_about_title">About NukeApp-OSS</string>
    <string name="manager_about_architecture">NukeApp-OSS provides XP82, libxposed API 102 and Zygisk entries with shared scheduling; APK patching is provided by the separate NukePatcher app.</string>

